<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Truso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th–10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Truso was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> trading settlement on the shore of Lake Drużno near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elblag">Elbląg</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, active from the 8th to the 10th century. The traveller Wulfstan, whose voyage from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hedeby">Hedeby</a> is recorded in the Old English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orosius">Orosius</a>, described sailing there around 890. Excavations at Janów Pomorski since 1982 have identified the site and found evidence of crafts, coins and long-distance trade.</p></div>
